      <description>Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi and French football star Kylian Mbappe have little in common, save perhaps the occasional boast about their hardcore work ethic. One is responsible for the world’s fourth-largest economy, home to 122 million people; the other answers to club management (and, to be fair, the French nation during the World Cup). But they’ve both found themselves on the wrong side of Beijing for saying something the Chinese state would rather nobody said.</description>
